    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field following this project's established pattern for derived, read-only owner fields (like `locality` and `timezone`):\n\n1. **`OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 a helper in `rest/function/owner/` with `forOwner(Owner)` that computes `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n   - TIER = `PREMIUM` when `owner.getMembershipLevel() >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - AREA = `METRO` when `OwnerLocality.forOwner(owner)` is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL` \u2014 reusing the existing locality derivation.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression for `ownerSegment`, wrapping the helper result in the generated `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum.fromValue(...)` (the OpenAPI enum type needs an explicit conversion in expression-based mappings).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` property to the Owner schema as a read-only string enum (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), which generates the `OwnerSegmentEnum` used above.\n\nBoth spec examples confirm correct behavior: a level-2 owner in Sydney (NSW) \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, and a level-2 owner in an unknown city \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`.",
